      "id": "step-3-python-toolkit",
      "title": "Python Package — Toolkit & Tools",
      "description": "The Python package lives in libs/langchain-nia/ and is built with Hatchling. The entry point is langchain_nia/__init__.py which exports all 20 tool classes. The NiaToolkit in toolkit.py aggregates tools into configurable groups — search, sources, GitHub, contexts, and dependencies — so agents can load only what they need. Each tool inherits from LangChain's BaseTool with Pydantic input schemas and both sync (_run) and async (_arun) methods.",
